// Thoughts: what grungo says, scrolled once across the dish. A row is a line
// and the condition under which he might say it. Two kinds share the table:
//
//   topic none   a thought. Now and then, between quiet gaps, the highest
//                priority whose condition holds wins (ties: the seeded draw).
//                kUrgentThought and up are in-the-moment and cut a gap short.
//   topic <t>    a prophecy (topics.def). Every shake, he foretells instead
//                of hopping: a draw weighted by the oracle's weight for the topic times
//                (1 + priority), over the rows whose condition holds.
//
//   when       a predicate in thoughts.cpp (rows may share one). It may set a
//              number, which the text shows in place of its '#'.
//   cooldownS  seconds before the same row may show again.
//   text       capitals, digits, space and . , ! ? - ' : (the renderer's
//              font), at most kMaxThoughtText characters; thoughts.h checks.
//              His voice (voices.def) frames it when it is said.
//
// Ids are stable: never renumber, never reuse.
// BLORB_THOUGHT(id, name, topic, when, priority, cooldownS, text)
BLORB_THOUGHT( 0, peckish,        none,   hungry,        3,  600, "SNACK? SNACK. THE GOOD BITS!")
